# GAMBIT YourMove — environment
#
# Copy to .env.local (git-ignored) and fill in ONE of the two backends below.
# The app validates this on the first request and fails with a named error if
# neither is complete. It never falls back to fixture data because a key is
# missing.
#
# Confirm the backend works before writing any feature code:
#     npm run verify:model
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Option A — Gemini API. Fastest to start.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Get a key at https://aistudio.google.com
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Option B — Vertex AI. Better for the Cloud Run deployment.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# On Cloud Run this authenticates with the service account attached to the
# service, so there is no API key sitting in an environment variable at all.
# That is a real difference for a judge reading the architecture, not just a
# preference.
#
# Leave GEMINI_API_KEY empty when using this path — env.ts checks the Vertex
# flag first, but an unused secret in a file is still a secret in a file.
#
# Local setup:
#     gcloud auth application-default login
#     gcloud services enable aiplatform.googleapis.com --project <your-project>
#
# On Cloud Run: grant the service's runtime service account permission to call
# Vertex AI models (the Vertex AI User role covers it; confirm against your
# org's policy, which may be narrower).
#
# GOOGLE_GENAI_USE_VERTEXAI=true
# GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT=your-project-id
# GOOGLE_CLOUD_LOCATION=us-central1
#
# The SDK parameter names behind these variables (vertexai / project /
# location) were read directly from @google/adk@1.6.0's type definitions. The
# gcloud steps above are the standard path and have NOT been executed from
# this repository — if one of them is wrong for your project, fix it here and
# note it in docs/journal.md.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Fixture mode — OPT-IN ONLY
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# When true, /api/read returns a stored fixture and calls no model. Every
# response is tagged mode:"mock" and the UI shows a visible badge, so a fixture
# can never be mistaken for a live read. Use it to work on the interface
# without a key, and as a rehearsed demo path if the venue network fails.
# GAMBIT_MOCK=true

# Extra per-request latency lines in the server log.
# GAMBIT_TELEMETRY_VERBOSE=true

# Base URL used by `npm run calibrate:read`. Defaults to http://localhost:3000.
# GAMBIT_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3000
